--- Exchange Online

Exchange Online is Microsoft's cloud-hosted email and calendaring service within Microsoft 365.

It provides:

Mailboxes
Email
Calendars
Contacts
Email delivery
----- Outlook vs Exchange Online
Outlook

Outlook is a client/application used to access:

Email
Calendar
Contacts
Mailbox features
Exchange Online

Exchange Online is the cloud service that provides:

Mailboxes
Email infrastructure
Calendaring
Email delivery
Memory
Outlook
↓
Client

Exchange Online
↓
Cloud email service
------ Shared Mailbox

A shared mailbox allows multiple authorized users to access a common mailbox.

Example:

support@company.com
        ↓
IT Support Team

Common examples:

support@
sales@
HR@

Users may receive permissions such as:

Read/access
Send As
Send on Behalf
---. Microsoft 365 License

A Microsoft 365 license determines which Microsoft 365 services and features a user is entitled to access based on the assigned plan and service configuration.

Possible services include:

Exchange Online
Teams
OneDrive
SharePoint
Office applications
Help Desk Scenario

If a user cannot access Teams, possible causes could include:

Authentication problem
MFA problem
License/service assignment
Network problem
Application problem
Microsoft 365 service issue

The license should be investigated rather than assumed to be the cause.

--- Microsoft 365 Admin Center

At an entry-level Help Desk level, understand that the Microsoft 365 Admin Center provides centralized administration for areas such as:

Users
Groups
Licenses
Services
Service health
Organization settings

Advanced administration is outside the current beginner roadmap.
